From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:17:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qcwcn: gate wpa_supplicant.conf on BOARD_WLAN_DEVICE

This prebuilt_etc is unconditional, while the identically named one in
hardware/broadcom/wlan/bcmdhd/config is gated on board_wlan_device. A
Qualcomm SoC with Broadcom Wi-Fi therefore defines the module twice and
kati refuses the build:

  base_rules.mk:320: error: hardware/qcom-caf/wlan/qcwcn/config:
  MODULE.TARGET.ETC.wpa_supplicant.conf already defined by
  hardware/broadcom/wlan/bcmdhd/config.

Adds the same guard with "qcwcn", so each tree contributes the file only
for the driver actually in use. Devices on qcwcn are unaffected.
---
 qcwcn/config/Android.bp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qcwcn/config/Android.bp b/qcwcn/config/Android.bp
index a0f4eb5..81a4b27 100644
--- a/qcwcn/config/Android.bp
+++ b/qcwcn/config/Android.bp
@@ -17,6 +17,10 @@ prebuilt_etc {
     src: ":wpa_supplicant_conf_gen",
     sub_dir: "wifi",
     vendor: true,
+    enabled: select(soong_config_variable("wpa_supplicant_8", "board_wlan_device"), {
+        "qcwcn": true,
+        default: false,
+    }),
     licenses: [
         "external_wpa_supplicant_8_license",
     ],
